Z||000031||fotofrank||10-06-2000||01:26 PM||||Oboy,Oboy,Oboy, headlight wars. I can't wait to get my 2 cents in...(LOL) . So when we look in an auto parts store for driving lights or fog lights do any of us read the box they come in? I have looked at a lot of lights and fond that few are labled DOT approved. Most clearly state (if you look for it) "for off road use only". Seems to me the manufacturer is saying that the lights they are selling are NOT street legal. Does this help answer the question of what is leagal and what is not. The use of a given light may not be the determining factor in legality but lumans and light pattern may take presedance. (wish i cud sple)<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||8
